    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0520" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg424"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Baron de Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 524.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In reply to your note of the 23d
                    ultimo, I have the honor to inclose proof sheets of the testimony given by Mr.
                    Rossi before the United States Industrial Commission.</p>
                <p>The secretary of the commission advises the Department that the proofs have not
                    been revised by Mr. Rossi, and that they are furnished as an exception to the
                    general rule in advance of their being printed for general distribution.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
